        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" data-w="75.9" style="background:rgba(139,92,246,.55)"><span>75.9%</span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bar-row">
        <div class="bar-label">Qwen3-8B (potential teacher)</div>
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" data-w="88.4" style="background:rgba(6,182,212,.55)"><span>88.4%</span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bar-row">
        <div class="bar-label">Qwen3-14B (potential teacher)</div>
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" data-w="89.5" style="background:rgba(6,182,212,.55)"><span>89.5%</span></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="bar-section-label">AIME 2024 (avg@16) — harder benchmark</div>
    <div class="results-bars">
      <div class="bar-row">
        <div class="bar-label">Qwen3-1.7B (deployment student)</div>
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" data-w="19.8" style="background:rgba(139,92,246,.55)"><span>19.8%</span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bar-row">
        <div class="bar-label">Qwen3-8B (potential teacher)</div>
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" data-w="47.7" style="background:rgba(6,182,212,.55)"><span>47.7%</span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bar-row">
        <div class="bar-label">Qwen3-14B (potential teacher)</div>
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" data-w="47.1" style="background:rgba(6,182,212,.55)"><span>47.1%</span></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<p>
  On AIME, the 8B model gets 47.7% — more than double the 1.7B's 19.8%. That gap is exactly the exploration headroom the paper exploits: spend the labeled data on the 8B to make it even better at finding correct reasoning chains, then transfer that behavior to the 1.7B via dense supervision.
</p>

<div class="callout c-purple">
  <span class="callout-icon">💡</span>
  <div class="callout-body">
    <strong>The allocation question:</strong> Given a fixed pool of labeled math problems, is it better to run GRPO on the 1.7B deployment student, or to run GRPO on the 8B teacher and then distill? The paper's answer: teacher-first, always — but only if the teacher has actually been RL-shaped first.
  </div>
</div>
